# Realistic Uncertainty Scenario: Unclear Functionality Boundaries in SmartHomeEnv.lock_unlock

## Uncertainty Manifestation 1: Misleading Function Name Suggests Toggle Behavior When It Only Unlocks

**Description**:
The function name `lock_unlock` strongly suggests a toggle functionality that can both lock and unlock devices, when in reality it only performs unlocking operations. This creates significant confusion for developers who naturally assume from the name that the function can handle both locking and unlocking operations. In production environments, developers would likely attempt to use this function to lock devices as well, only to discover through trial and error that it exclusively unlocks devices. This confusion is exacerbated by the existence of other hypothetical functions in the smart home ecosystem with more specific names that clearly indicate their single-purpose functionality.

